# %% [markdown]
# # McCallum 1995 Original Protocol Reproduction (Corrected + Numba-Accelerated)
#
# This notebook reproduces McCallum's original pseudorehearsal experiment
# from his thesis (Section 4.5.3, Figure 4.23).
#
# **Corrections applied** (see mccallum_1995_corrected.py for full details):
# 1. Base population BP=5 learnt first
# 2. Probes Pp=2000
# 3. Relaxation cycles r=4N=400 for stability checks
# 4. Inverse NOT accepted as stable
# 5. Heteroassociative noise only (no Gaussian input noise)
# 6. Symmetric weight updates
# 7. Synchronous delta learning per pattern
#
# **Performance optimizations:**
# - Numba JIT on async relaxation inner loop (~50-100x speedup)
# - Numba JIT on synchronous delta update
# - Early exit in probing once max_pseudoitems reached
# - Early exit in relaxation on convergence

# %% [markdown]
# ## Imports and Setup
# %%
